course: dictionary
lesson: 15221
title: Sequential: one after another
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sequential means coming in a set order, one thing after another. Look for clue words like first, next, then and last. They show the order. «First wash the apples, next cut them, then put them in the bowl.» Each step waits for the one before it.
explain: Sequential numbers follow a pattern. «The tickets are numbered 4, 5, 6 and 7.» Each number is one more than the last, so the numbers are sequential. In maths, you can spot the pattern and say what comes next.
explain: Use the context to check. Ask yourself: do these things happen in a set order? If they do, sequential fits. Then swap in your meaning, such as «one after another, in order», and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Sequential means coming one after another in a fixed order.
fact: Sequentially is the adverb: «The lights came on sequentially, one after another.»
fact: Sequential steps are done step by step, finishing one step before starting the next.
fact: In computing, a program carries out its sequential steps in order, from first to last.
fact: Sequential numbers, like 4, 5, 6, go up by one each time.
exercise: «The steps in the recipe are sequential.» What does sequential mean here? | Only for very fast cooks | Done all at once in a messy pile | Written in pencil | *Done one after another in a set order
exercise: «The tickets were sequentially numbered: 12, 13, 14.» What does sequentially numbered mean? | Numbered in red ink | Numbered at random, with no pattern | *Numbered in order, each one one more than the last | Every ticket has the same number
exercise: Which list shows sequential numbers? | 10, 40, 4, 100 | 9, 2, 7, 1 | 5, 5, 8, 1 | *2, 3, 4, 5
test: Sam follows sequential instructions: mix, then bake, then cool. What does sequential mean here? | The steps all happen at the same time | *Each step happens in order, one after another | Sam can skip the steps he does not like
test: Which phrase is closest in meaning to sequential? | Very quick | *One after another | In a circle | Mixed up
exam: Ella says, «The lights flashed sequentially: red, then yellow, then green.» What does sequentially mean? | *One after another, in a fixed order | Mixed up at random | All at once in a bright flash | Only at night
